# An odd mirror at the centre selects the first higher-order mode. Below the cut-off width the solver returns a box mode under the cladding index.
# Reference: the same grid solved with a sparse eigen-solver in SciPy.
title Silicon strip 500 x 220 nm, first antisymmetric quasi-TE mode
grid dx=0.025 dy=0.02
window width=3.0 ymin=-1.0 ymax=1.22
rect si -0.25 0.25 0 0.22
symmetry odd
field te
expect neff 1.454724316 2e-8
expect confinement 0.110827779 1e-6
expect guided yes
expect cells 6660
